{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 12,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "No doubt but ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the people, and wisdom shall die with you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I have understanding as well as you; I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not inferior to you: yes, who knoweth not such things as these?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " one mocked by his neighbor, who calleth upon God, and he answereth him: the just upright ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " derided.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that is ready to slip with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " feet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a lamp despised in the thought of him that is at ease.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The tabernacles of robbers prosper, and they that provoke God are secure; into whose hand God bringeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "abundantly",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ask now the beasts, and they shall teach thee; and the fowls of the air, and they shall tell thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or speak to the earth, and it shall teach thee: and the fishes of the sea shall declare to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who knoweth not in all these that the hand of the LORD hath wrought this?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In whose hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the soul of every living thing, and the breath of all mankind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth not the ear try words? and the mouth taste its food?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With the ancient ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom; and in length of days understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom and strength, he hath counsel and understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he breaketh down, and it cannot be built again: he shutteth up a man, and there can be no opening.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he withholdeth the waters, and they dry up: also he sendeth them out, and they overturn the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strength and wisdom: the deceived and the deceiver ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He leadeth counselors away spoiled, and maketh the judges fools.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He looseth the bond of kings, and girdeth their loins with a girdle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He leadeth princes away spoiled, and overthroweth the mighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He removeth away the speech of the trusty, and taketh away the understanding of the aged.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He poureth contempt upon princes, and weakeneth the strength of the mighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He revealeth deep things out of darkness, and bringeth to light the shades of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He increaseth nations, and destroyeth them: he enlargeth nations, and straiteneth them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "again",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He taketh away the heart of the chief of the people of the earth, and causeth them to wander in a wilderness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "where there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.12.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.12.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They grope in the dark without light, and he maketh them to stagger like ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " drunken ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
